Only the $x$ component of the <vector field> is nonzero, so $\mathbf F\cdot d\mathbf r=(x^2+y^2)\,dx$. On the vertical segment, $dx=0$ throughout. Hence
$$
\boxed{\int_C\mathbf F\cdot d\mathbf r=0}.
$$

= b
{parent=9}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=b}

On the horizontal segment $y=0$, while $x$ decreases from $1$ to $-1$. Keeping this orientation gives
$$
\boxed{\int_C\mathbf F\cdot d\mathbf r=\int_1^{-1}x^2\,dx=-\frac23}.
$$
The minus sign follows from traversing opposite to the positive $x$ direction.

