The support is $x\geq1$, and its normalized <Pareto distribution> density integrates to
$$
\boxed{P(X\geq1)=\int_1^\infty\alpha x^{-\alpha-1}\,dx
=\left[-x^{-\alpha}\right]_1^\infty=1}.
$$

= b
{parent=10}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=b}

Integrate the <probability density function> over the specified interval:
$$
\boxed{P(2\leq X\leq3)=\int_2^3\alpha x^{-\alpha-1}\,dx
=2^{-\alpha}-3^{-\alpha}}.
$$
The endpoint inclusions make no difference for this continuous distribution.

